  "worked_solution": "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $\u03a0$ is $n=\u27e80,12,-6\u27e9.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $\u03a0$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12y-6z-30 & =0 \\\\ -6z & =-12y+30 \\\\ z & =2y-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $y=0$, we get $z=-5.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-5)$ lies on $\u03a0.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=\u27e80,0,-5\u27e9.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-\u27e80,0,-5\u27e9)\\cdot \u27e80,12,-6\u27e9 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
